WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:05.381
Iggy. tell me what's going on. Please!

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:09.260
Someone in our outfit's been
sharing secrets with Rupert Thorne.

3
00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:12.763
You wouldn't happen to know anything
about that. would you. Clarence?

4
00:00:12.847 --> 00:00:17.852
What. you think it's me? Come on. Iggy.
You and me. we go way back.

5
00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:19.937
You know I'd never do that.

6
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.523
Sure. Sure. Clarence.

7
00:00:22.606 --> 00:00:25.234
But the boss would like
to have a word with you anyway.

8
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:28.362
No. Iggy. come on.

9
00:00:28.446 --> 00:00:29.905
Please. no!

10
00:00:31.157 --> 00:00:34.785
I don't know who told you I wasn't
on the level. but you gotta believe me.

11
00:00:34.869 --> 00:00:35.870
I'd never...

12
00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:38.038
No!

13
00:00:38.831 --> 00:00:40.833
No!

14
00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:43.335
Come on. hurry it up. Double time.

15
00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:46.589
- We need all this stuff out of here now!
- Why the big rush?

16
00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:48.734
Mr. Thorne says it looks like
we're going to get hit tonight.

17
00:00:48.758 --> 00:00:51.010
and the swag's too valuable
to leave behind.

18
00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:55.139
What. the cops? The boss has half
the precinct on the payroll.

19
00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.975
Yeah. But it ain't the cops
I'm worried about.

20
00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:01.437
Oh. not you too.
That story's a load of bull.

21
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.357
- Marvin saw it last week.
- Marvin. who's in the hospital?

22
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:07.610
Yeah. How do you think he got there?

23
00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:10.905
Well. then he's got a screw loose
because there ain't no friggin'...

24
00:01:10.988 --> 00:01:12.531
- What?
- Shut up!

25
00:01:13.532 --> 00:01:15.701
Someone's in here with us.

26
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

27
00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:54.031
You stupid...

28
00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.442
Three explosions in two weeks.

29
00:03:11.525 --> 00:03:13.944
All three buildings can be traced
to shadow companies

30
00:03:14.028 --> 00:03:15.779
operated by Rupert Thorne.

31
00:03:15.863 --> 00:03:18.574
The police ruled
the first explosion a gas leak.

32
00:03:18.657 --> 00:03:22.828
the second...
an accidental electrical fire.

33
00:03:22.912 --> 00:03:26.624
Someone's declared war on Thorne.
but they're covering their tracks.

34
00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:28.125
Being smart about it.

35
00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:31.253
That would suggest there's a crime boss
we don't know about.

36
00:03:31.337 --> 00:03:33.923
One who's bold enough
to take on Rupert Thorne.

37
00:03:34.006 --> 00:03:36.800
But if that's the case.
we could be looking at...

38
00:03:36.884 --> 00:03:39.178
An all-out gang war
on the streets of Gotham.

39
00:03:39.261 --> 00:03:40.304
Good Lord.

40
00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.806
I need to find out
who's behind these explosions.

41
00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:45.059
And I know where
to start looking for them.

42
00:03:45.142 --> 00:03:46.560
Police headquarters?

43
00:03:46.644 --> 00:03:49.939
You think someone inside the department
is covering up these explosions?

44
00:03:50.022 --> 00:03:51.857
It's Gotham. Pennyworth.

45
00:03:51.941 --> 00:03:54.902
Does the corruption really surprise you?

46
00:03:55.861 --> 00:03:57.905
Ladies and gentlemen of the jury.

47
00:03:57.988 --> 00:04:02.242
with all due respect.
the prosecution's case is absurd.

48
00:04:02.326 --> 00:04:05.704
My client isn't the mastermind
behind a smuggling ring.

49
00:04:05.788 --> 00:04:07.331
He isn't a killer.

50
00:04:07.414 --> 00:04:11.877
He's a desperate kid who took
the wrong job from the wrong people.

51
00:04:11.961 --> 00:04:13.545
It's as simple as that.

52
00:04:15.381 --> 00:04:18.884
Court will recess
until the jury reaches a verdict.

53
00:04:24.932 --> 00:04:28.394
It was a good closer. Miss Gordon.
But you know you're gonna lose. right?

54
00:04:28.477 --> 00:04:31.355
- I had that jury eating out of my hand.
- Come on.

55
00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:33.691
You know this kid's been set up
to take the fall.

56
00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:36.276
Well. then he should have squealed
on his bosses.

57
00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.028
Not my fault he wouldn't take a deal.

58
00:04:38.112 --> 00:04:40.364
And I suppose it's not your fault
my key witness

59
00:04:40.447 --> 00:04:42.366
took a sudden trip to Bermuda either?

60
00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:45.411
I'm sure I don't know
what you're talking about. Barbara.

61
00:04:45.494 --> 00:04:48.122
And I'm sure you do. Harvey.

62
00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:50.457
It's all politics for you now.

63
00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:53.168
Every conviction.
another ad for your campaign.

64
00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:55.587
"Harvey Dent: Tough On Crime."

65
00:04:55.671 --> 00:04:57.339
Hey. I'm just doing my job.

66
00:04:57.423 --> 00:05:00.843
If putting hardened criminals behind bars
helps me in the polls. then...

67
00:05:00.926 --> 00:05:01.969
Oh. that reminds me.

68
00:05:02.052 --> 00:05:04.388
- Here. hot off the presses.
- No. thanks.

69
00:05:04.471 --> 00:05:06.890
Give it to someone
who might actually vote for you.

70
00:05:06.974 --> 00:05:09.143
Oh. come on. I'm not that bad.

71
00:05:09.226 --> 00:05:11.687
Look. I'll even give your kid a break.

72
00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.858
Heads. I'll ask for 20 years to life.
Tails. he gets the chair.

73
00:05:15.941 --> 00:05:19.028
I'm not betting a man's life
on a coin flip.

74
00:05:19.111 --> 00:05:22.614
- You're an ass. Dent!
- Oh. don't go away mad.

75
00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:26.160
Look. heads. You won!

76
00:06:13.665 --> 00:06:15.250
Crap.

77
00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:16.960
Ah!

78
00:06:20.923 --> 00:06:25.344
Help! Help me! Someone...

79
00:06:25.427 --> 00:06:27.596
Who's behind those explosions?

80
00:06:27.679 --> 00:06:31.183
Oh. God. Who... what are you?

81
00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:35.145
Three buildings blown to pieces.
You falsified the reports.

82
00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:36.230
Who paid you?

83
00:06:36.313 --> 00:06:37.665
Are you crazy?

84
00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:38.689
Pull me up!

85
00:06:38.732 --> 00:06:41.652
- Give me a name.
- Just pull me up!

86
00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:44.071
Oh. God! Hurry. please!

87
00:06:44.154 --> 00:06:47.699
- I won't ask again.
- It was the Penguin!

88
00:06:47.783 --> 00:06:50.369
It was the freakin' Penguin!

89
00:06:51.703 --> 00:06:55.707
Oh. God. Oh. my God.

90
00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:59.002
If you're lying to me. I'll be back.

91
00:07:04.299 --> 00:07:07.469
It was... it was the Penguin.

92
00:07:07.553 --> 00:07:10.013
<i>It was the freakin' Penguin!</i>

93
00:07:11.014 --> 00:07:15.060
<i>♪ I know I've done you wrong ♪</i>

94
00:07:15.144 --> 00:07:17.479
<i>♪ Remember that rainy eve ♪</i>

95
00:07:17.563 --> 00:07:20.607
<i>♪ That I drove you out ♪</i>

96
00:07:20.691 --> 00:07:25.237
<i>♪ With nothing but a fine-tooth comb ♪</i>

97
00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.073
<i>♪ And no one to blame ♪</i>

98
00:07:28.157 --> 00:07:30.576
<i>♪ Well. ain't that a shame ♪</i>

99
00:07:30.659 --> 00:07:36.165
<i>♪ Bill Bailey
Won't you please come home. come home? ♪</i>

100
00:07:36.248 --> 00:07:38.834
<i>♪ Bill Bailey. won't you please ♪</i>

101
00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:43.797
<i>♪ Come home ♪</i>

102
00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:49.761
Oh. thank you. Thank you.

103
00:07:53.307 --> 00:07:57.269
Hello. If it isn't Detective Arnold Flass.

104
00:07:57.352 --> 00:08:01.315
Mm-mm. sugar.
You can frisk me any day of the week.

105
00:08:01.398 --> 00:08:05.277
Hey. me next! Do me next!

106
00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:08.155
Not if you were the last cop
on the force. Bullock.

107
00:08:08.238 --> 00:08:10.908
Mwah!

108
00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:14.703
23 Skidoo. I bid you <i>adieu.</i>

109
00:08:19.082 --> 00:08:23.003
To think I could be at home about now.
doing my nails.

110
00:08:23.086 --> 00:08:26.506
Or the dishes or my taxes.

111
00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:29.426
It's not like I'm having fun here
either. Barbara.

112
00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:32.596
But the commissioner can't exactly
skip a police fundraiser.

113
00:08:32.679 --> 00:08:35.807
Well. so long as we're both miserable.

114
00:08:35.891 --> 00:08:38.894
Thanks for humoring your old man.

115
00:08:38.977 --> 00:08:40.604
Anytime. Dad.

116
00:08:40.687 --> 00:08:44.191
It doesn't bother you that half
these people want to see you fail?

117
00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:46.193
Oh. come on. honey.

118
00:08:46.276 --> 00:08:48.403
I'm sure it's far more than half.

119
00:08:48.487 --> 00:08:50.864
- Commissioner Gordon.
- Harvey.

120
00:08:50.948 --> 00:08:53.784
- You know my daughter.
- Know her? If I had my way.

121
00:08:53.867 --> 00:08:56.662
this little spitfire would
be working for me in the DA's office.

122
00:08:56.745 --> 00:08:59.248
You know. Jim. once I'm elected mayor.

123
00:08:59.331 --> 00:09:01.625
you and I are going to do great things
for this city.

124
00:09:01.708 --> 00:09:03.752
Yeah. absolutely.

125
00:09:03.835 --> 00:09:07.589
Who knows? Maybe then you won't
need outside help from giant bats.

126
00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:11.385
So you're buying into rumors
off the streets now. Harvey?

127
00:09:11.468 --> 00:09:13.804
Do you leave cookies out for Santa too?

128
00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:17.975
What'd I tell you. Jim? Spitfire.

129
00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:20.602
I've suspected the <i>Iceberg</i>
was some kind of front

130
00:09:20.686 --> 00:09:23.480
for smuggling guns or drugs or worse.

131
00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:25.524
But to take on Rupert Thorne...

132
00:09:25.607 --> 00:09:28.819
Yes. it would appear
you've underestimated the Penguin. sir.

133
00:09:28.902 --> 00:09:30.946
Everyone has. That's how she wants it.

134
00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:36.326
Flashy cabaret act. gambling ship.
hiding in plain sight. Smart.

135
00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:41.123
Nice spread. huh?

136
00:09:41.206 --> 00:09:43.208
Well. that's Mama for you.

137
00:09:43.292 --> 00:09:47.337
Us Cobblepots
are all about style.

138
00:09:47.421 --> 00:09:50.465
Hm. Say. sweetie.
You really ought to try the shrimp.

139
00:09:50.549 --> 00:09:53.093
Mm! So yummy.

140
00:09:53.176 --> 00:09:56.972
- You have cocktail sauce on your shirt.
- Nuts!

141
00:09:57.055 --> 00:10:00.434
Well. uh.
guess my shirt got a little hungry.

142
00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.854
Stuck-up little...

143
00:10:03.937 --> 00:10:05.272
Not even that pretty. anyway.

144
00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:07.691
Smooth. Ronnie. Real smooth.

145
00:10:07.774 --> 00:10:10.235
And you wonder
why Mama calls you the slow one.

146
00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:12.946
Oh. go climb your thumb. half pint.

147
00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:15.407
Do enjoy the party. Master Bruce.

148
00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:18.827
- Was that a joke?
- I suppose.

149
00:10:20.329 --> 00:10:21.997
Oh. it's Bruce Wayne!

150
00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.084
Well. this is embarrassing.
You started the party without me.

151
00:10:26.168 --> 00:10:30.130
- You made it. Bruce.
- And so did you. um...

152
00:10:30.213 --> 00:10:32.758
It's... it's Aaron.
This is my mama's party.

153
00:10:32.841 --> 00:10:37.596
Oh. that's swell. Say. Alan. be a pal
and find a spot for these.

154
00:10:38.513 --> 00:10:41.391
Bruce! Late as always.

155
00:10:41.475 --> 00:10:42.702
What was the problem this time?

156
00:10:42.726 --> 00:10:45.562
Harvey. the only problem
is that you and I are at a party.

157
00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:48.023
and neither of us has a drink.

158
00:10:50.442 --> 00:10:53.987
Rupert Thorne.
What a lovely surprise.

159
00:10:54.071 --> 00:10:55.864
I didn't expect you to show.

160
00:10:55.947 --> 00:11:01.119
I wouldn't miss it. Supporting
local law enforcement is our civic duty.

161
00:11:01.203 --> 00:11:03.163
True. So true.

162
00:11:03.246 --> 00:11:07.042
I must say. I was devastated
to hear another of your properties

163
00:11:07.125 --> 00:11:08.460
exploded the other night.

164
00:11:08.543 --> 00:11:12.631
Did I hear you had an office
in that building? Heavens!

165
00:11:12.714 --> 00:11:16.510
If you'd been there. why.
you would have been blown to pieces.

166
00:11:16.593 --> 00:11:19.513
Itty-bitty pieces.

167
00:11:19.596 --> 00:11:23.183
Actually. Oswalda. I was there.

168
00:11:23.266 --> 00:11:28.563
Lucky for me. I got a tip and
hightailed it out of there just in time.

169
00:11:28.647 --> 00:11:31.775
Oh? A tip. you say?

170
00:11:31.858 --> 00:11:35.654
Indeed. You might say
a little birdie told me.

171
00:11:37.614 --> 00:11:41.201
Itty bitty birdie.

172
00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:43.954
See you around. Penguin.

173
00:11:45.539 --> 00:11:49.000
So the duchess says.
"No. not on the first date."

174
00:11:49.084 --> 00:11:52.003
Oh. for Pete's sake.

175
00:11:52.087 --> 00:11:55.841
Guess I can't hold my liquor.
Be right back.

176
00:12:34.087 --> 00:12:37.424
Well. Mama.
I'd say your little shindig

177
00:12:37.507 --> 00:12:40.385
is a big success.

178
00:12:40.469 --> 00:12:44.473
Indeed. Buttercup.
It's been quite an evening.

179
00:12:44.556 --> 00:12:46.933
Just full of surprises.

180
00:12:51.563 --> 00:12:54.858
Guess it's not a yacht party
until someone falls overboard.

181
00:12:54.941 --> 00:12:56.818
Uh-huh. Excuse me.

182
00:12:56.902 --> 00:13:00.238
Bruce Wayne! What happened to you?

183
00:13:00.322 --> 00:13:03.450
Guess it's not a yacht party
until someone falls overboard.

184
00:13:05.327 --> 00:13:08.955
So. how much you figure we cleared
off all these dumb coppers anyway?

185
00:13:09.039 --> 00:13:12.083
The exact amount
almost doesn't matter. darling.

186
00:13:12.167 --> 00:13:14.419
Embezzling thousands from Gotham's finest

187
00:13:14.503 --> 00:13:18.924
right under their stupid noses
is a treasure in and of itself.

188
00:13:21.259 --> 00:13:24.679
But I'll tell you what made
tonight truly unforgettable.

189
00:13:24.763 --> 00:13:29.017
It was learning that one of my sweet.
precious. little angels

190
00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:32.604
sold me out.

191
00:13:32.687 --> 00:13:35.482
- Wait. What? No. Mama. We never...
- It was Aaron!

192
00:13:35.565 --> 00:13:37.567
- It had to be him!
- What? Come on!

193
00:13:37.651 --> 00:13:40.445
Ronnie's the one who's always
saying crap behind your back!

194
00:13:40.529 --> 00:13:43.782
You lousy. butt-kissing. snot-nosed punk!
I oughta break your neck!

195
00:13:43.865 --> 00:13:46.409
Boys. boys. please.

196
00:13:46.493 --> 00:13:49.287
Mama already knows which one of you it is.

197
00:13:51.081 --> 00:13:54.334
No! No. I didn't.
You found the rat. Mama.

198
00:13:54.417 --> 00:13:58.380
Yeah. He said it was that Clarence guy.
It wasn't me. I swear. it wasn't me.

199
00:13:58.463 --> 00:14:01.466
- Sounds kind of guilty. don't he. Mama?
- You shut up!

200
00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.094
Did you. uh. remember to eat something
at the party. Mama?

201
00:14:04.177 --> 00:14:08.056
'Cause I know you get a little testy
sometimes when you're hungry.

202
00:14:08.139 --> 00:14:10.600
Please. Mama. Please. don't.

203
00:14:10.684 --> 00:14:14.980
- No. please!
- It's okay. baby.

204
00:14:15.063 --> 00:14:17.774
You know Mama never holds a grudge...

205
00:14:18.692 --> 00:14:20.277
...for long.

206
00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:23.738
Wait! Wait. wait. wait! No!

207
00:14:23.822 --> 00:14:26.950
Mama! No! Please!

208
00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:40.046
He was my favorite.

209
00:14:41.256 --> 00:14:43.550
Guess that makes you my favorite now.

210
00:14:50.932 --> 00:14:53.393
- Thorne.
<i>- Mr. Thorne. Mama's onto us.</i>

211
00:14:53.476 --> 00:14:54.996
<i>She thought it was Aaron
who tipped you off.</i>

212
00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.188
But she's gonna figure out it's me.
You gotta help me!

213
00:14:57.272 --> 00:15:00.775
<i>Sorry. sonny.</i>

214
00:15:00.859 --> 00:15:04.904
I don't think you're the kind of man
I want in my organization.

215
00:15:04.988 --> 00:15:08.074
Hell. you just sold out your own mother.
for God's sake.

216
00:15:08.158 --> 00:15:10.827
Wait. wait. wait. But you... you promised.

217
00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.872
- What am I gonna do?
<i>- Not my problem. kid.</i>

218
00:15:13.955 --> 00:15:15.790
<i>Bye now.</i>

219
00:15:18.126 --> 00:15:20.295
<i>What do you mean. gone?</i>

220
00:15:20.378 --> 00:15:22.631
Looks like he took one of the motorboats.

221
00:15:22.714 --> 00:15:25.300
Do you have any idea what this means?

222
00:15:25.383 --> 00:15:27.969
That Thorne got you to kill the wrong son?

223
00:15:28.053 --> 00:15:29.387
No!

224
00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:33.141
It means that brat's gonna squeal
about the whole operation.

225
00:15:33.224 --> 00:15:36.102
Whatever it takes. find him.

226
00:15:54.954 --> 00:15:58.541
Oh! Sweetie. Thank God.
I was hoping you'd be here.

227
00:15:58.625 --> 00:16:00.960
Call me that again.
and you're gonna lose some teeth.

228
00:16:01.044 --> 00:16:02.962
- What do you want?
- I need your help. sweet...

229
00:16:03.046 --> 00:16:06.341
Miss Gordon. She's gonna kill me.

230
00:16:06.424 --> 00:16:07.884
- My mama.
- What?

231
00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:10.178
She is not what she looks like.

232
00:16:10.261 --> 00:16:14.182
She runs a mob.
She's a scary lady! Please!

233
00:16:14.265 --> 00:16:15.975
- You gotta help me.
- Why me?

234
00:16:16.059 --> 00:16:20.230
Your dad's the only cop in Gotham
I know for sure isn't bent.

235
00:16:20.313 --> 00:16:22.691
Can you take me to see him?
I'll tell him everything.

236
00:16:22.774 --> 00:16:23.942
I'm busy.

237
00:16:24.025 --> 00:16:27.028
Mama just killed my brother
right in front of me!

238
00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:31.092
Oh. why did I have to pick Thorne
over my mother?

239
00:16:31.116 --> 00:16:32.659
I mean. what a sap I am!

240
00:16:32.742 --> 00:16:35.638
Who cares if she deserved it. or that
she's more of a monster than a mother?

241
00:16:35.662 --> 00:16:39.457
I just had to be a big shot. right?
Oh. always had to be a big shot!

242
00:16:39.541 --> 00:16:42.919
Hey. Ronald. how about you
stop the whining? At least until...

243
00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.216
Oh. God. she found me! I'm cooked!

244
00:16:49.801 --> 00:16:51.594
Okay. Hold on to something.

245
00:17:04.607 --> 00:17:09.028
Oh. God! Please. no. Mama! I'm sorry!
I'm so sorry. Mama!

246
00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:10.947
Knock it off! Here. take the wheel.

247
00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.700
- What?
- Take the damn wheel!

248
00:17:26.963 --> 00:17:28.339
Come on.

249
00:18:11.591 --> 00:18:14.219
I'm telling you.
we gotta leave right now.

250
00:18:14.302 --> 00:18:17.055
We gotta go somewhere else.
somewhere secret.

251
00:18:17.138 --> 00:18:19.432
Now. hold on. son. We can protect you.

252
00:18:19.516 --> 00:18:21.059
No. that was before.

253
00:18:21.142 --> 00:18:23.645
But now my mom is after me.
She knows! She knows!

254
00:18:23.728 --> 00:18:26.815
- You're in police custody. This isn't...
- Don't you get it?

255
00:18:26.898 --> 00:18:30.151
She's got cops on her payroll.
and one of them had to see me come in.

256
00:18:30.235 --> 00:18:32.797
- I'm telling you. we are not safe here.
- What are you talking about?

257
00:18:32.821 --> 00:18:35.532
- What's going on. Flass?
- You need to make a call.

258
00:18:35.615 --> 00:18:39.494
Thank you. Detective Bullock.
You've been most helpful.

259
00:18:39.577 --> 00:18:42.997
I'll see you and Flass
get an extra 50 this week.

260
00:18:45.041 --> 00:18:48.002
The little fink is spilling it
to Gordon right now.

261
00:18:48.086 --> 00:18:51.798
Let me have one of the insiders
take care of it. keep it quiet.

262
00:18:51.881 --> 00:18:55.093
No. it's too late for quiet.

263
00:18:56.135 --> 00:18:57.804
You don't know what she can do.

264
00:18:58.513 --> 00:19:00.849
<i>The woman is a criminal genius.</i>

265
00:19:00.932 --> 00:19:03.852
<i>She's been running rings
around you guys for months.</i>

266
00:19:03.935 --> 00:19:07.897
<i>You think Thorne's buildings are suddenly
blowing up all over town by accident?</i>

267
00:19:08.982 --> 00:19:13.486
<i>Mama bought herself a customized
military-grade. long-range cannon.</i>

268
00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:15.405
<i>She's got it rigged up on the</i> Iceberg.

269
00:19:15.488 --> 00:19:18.116
<i>With that thing. she could hit any place
in Gotham she wants:</i>

270
00:19:18.199 --> 00:19:20.994
<i>warehouses. apartments. police stations.</i>

271
00:19:21.077 --> 00:19:22.954
You get it now?

272
00:19:23.538 --> 00:19:25.516
I'll have the Coast Guard
bring in the <i>Iceberg.</i> Barbara!

273
00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:28.960
Everybody. out of the building now!

274
00:19:29.043 --> 00:19:30.503
Go!

275
00:19:53.151 --> 00:19:57.155
Hurry it up. We're bringing down
the house tonight. Chop. chop.

276
00:19:57.989 --> 00:20:00.575
Give me that. Taking too long.

277
00:20:06.497 --> 00:20:09.792
There. Okay. boys. let's load it up.

278
00:20:14.964 --> 00:20:18.801
Well. I'll be damned. Virginia.
There really is a Batman.

279
00:20:18.885 --> 00:20:23.348
- Iggy. break this jerk in half.
- Yes. ma'am.

280
00:20:55.755 --> 00:20:58.049
Scratch one police station.

281
00:21:00.885 --> 00:21:03.846
Okay. Dracula. You asked for it.

282
00:21:08.851 --> 00:21:12.105
Get out of my way! Get out of my way!
Come on. move it!

283
00:21:12.188 --> 00:21:13.648
Help me!

284
00:21:13.731 --> 00:21:17.652
The alarm went off. and that lousy cop
just up and left me sitting here!

285
00:21:17.735 --> 00:21:19.362
Okay. hang on.

286
00:21:23.074 --> 00:21:26.202
Attention!
This is the United States Coast Guard.

287
00:21:27.286 --> 00:21:29.956
Fun's over. freak. Get out of my way.

288
00:21:35.712 --> 00:21:36.963
Oof!

289
00:21:53.354 --> 00:21:54.480
I think that's everybody.

290
00:21:55.148 --> 00:21:56.774
Down!

291
00:22:04.907 --> 00:22:07.618
See that? And now we all...

292
00:22:09.454 --> 00:22:10.538
...lose.

293
00:22:11.914 --> 00:22:14.917
- Get that hose over here!
- Come on. let's go!

294
00:22:18.087 --> 00:22:22.300
- We got lucky.
- Yeah. But we moved fast too.

295
00:22:22.383 --> 00:22:26.095
- Made some of that luck on our own.
- Yeah. I guess so.

296
00:22:27.346 --> 00:22:30.266
Oh. that Batman guy is real. by the way.

297
00:22:31.225 --> 00:22:33.978
I met him tonight... sort of.

298
00:22:34.854 --> 00:22:36.564
He has a really nice car.

299
00:22:42.361 --> 00:22:47.075
Since you refuse to sleep. Master Bruce.
I insist you at least eat.

300
00:22:47.992 --> 00:22:51.120
I've been piecing together the full extent
of Penguin's empire.

301
00:22:51.204 --> 00:22:55.374
- Former empire. you mean?
- Yes. And that's the problem.

302
00:22:55.458 --> 00:22:57.794
Penguin was keeping Thorne's mob in check.

303
00:22:57.877 --> 00:23:00.671
By taking down her operation
in one fell swoop...

304
00:23:00.755 --> 00:23:03.549
You've just given another piece
of the city to Rupert Thorne.

305
00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:07.720
I failed tonight.
That can't happen again.

305
00:23:08.305 --> 00:24:08.342
